## PendingRegistration (Mologadi)

Note : if the Student / Organiser do Not have a password field, add it in now please. Created At and Expires At should not be in the builder, they should be default / auto created values

| Field | Type |
|---|---|
| `uuid` | String (PK, generated — not auto-increment) |
| `email` | String |
| `password` | String |
| `role` | String |
| `facultyId` | Long |
| `studentNumber` | String, nullable |
| `pin` | String |
| `expiresAt` | LocalDateTime |
| `createdAt` | LocalDateTime |

Builder pattern, same convention as every other entity. `PendingRegistrationRepository extends JpaRepository<PendingRegistration, String>` — note the ID type is `String` (the UUID), not `Long`.

**Factory usage timing:** at register time, call the existing `StudentFactory`/`OrganiserFactory` (already built in Milestone 1) purely to validate — the object it returns is discarded, never saved. At verify time — once PIN + expiry pass — call the same factory again with the fields pulled off the matched `PendingRegistration` row to build the real object, and that one gets saved.

**New repo method needed:** `existsByEmail(String Email)` on both `StudentRepository` and `OrganiserRepository`, for the duplicate check in `register()`. Plain method, not Query by Example against a whole object — matching the full candidate would treat two signups with the same username but different faculty/password as different people.

